---
import BuyerVerdict from '../../components/brands/BuyerVerdict.astro';
import {BUYER_VERDICTS} from '../../data/buyer-verdicts';
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import {BRAND_COMPARISONS} from '../../data/brand-comparisons';
import {MODEL_SPECS} from '../../data/model-specs';
export function getStaticPaths(){return BRAND_COMPARISONS.map(pair=>({params:{pair:pair.slug},props:{pair}}));}
const {pair}=Astro.props;
const models=pair.ids.map(id=>MODEL_SPECS.find(m=>m.modelId===id)!);
const fields=[['Selected configuration',(m:typeof models[number])=>m.modelId],['LP / NG rated kW',(m:typeof models[number])=>`${m.ratingsKw.LP??'Unknown'} / ${m.ratingsKw['Natural gas']??'Unknown'}`],['ATS scope',(m:typeof models[number])=>m.transferSwitch??'Not established'],['Warranty summary',(m:typeof models[number])=>m.warranty??'Not established'],['Starting published MSRP',(m:typeof models[number])=>m.startingMsrpUsd?'$'+m.startingMsrpUsd.toLocaleString('en-US')+'; '+m.startingMsrpNote:'No supported amount in this record'],['Monitoring',(m:typeof models[number])=>m.monitoring??'Not established'],['Evidence notes',(m:typeof models[number])=>{ const notes=m.evidenceNotes?.join(' ')||'No conflict recorded; unknown fields still apply.'; return notes.length>160?notes.slice(0,160).trimEnd()+'… (full notes on each model page)':notes; }]] as const;
---
<ArticleLayout title={pair.title+': Compare Exact Standby Configurations'} description={pair.focus} category="Comparisons" categoryHref="/comparisons/" published="2026-10-05" updated="2026-10-07" verified="2026-10-05" readingTime="6 min read" toc={[]} sources={models.flatMap(m=>m.sources.map(s=>({label:m.modelId+' — '+s.label,href:s.url,type:'Manufacturer' as const,verified:s.checkedOn})))}>
<BuyerVerdict a={pair.ids[0]} b={pair.ids[1]} fitA={BUYER_VERDICTS[pair.slug][0]} fitB={BUYER_VERDICTS[pair.slug][1]} skip="Pause either purchase if the proposal omits exact transfer equipment, fuel capacity, an installer-verified load plan or an identified service provider." change="A corrected model document, different installed scope, verified warranty terms or a better documented local service option." gaps="Comparable failure-rate evidence, local response times and equal-scope installed prices are not established."/>
<h2>The purchase question</h2><p>{pair.focus} {pair.question}</p><p>Published information supports a comparison of these selected configurations only. It does not establish a brand-wide reliability ranking. Independent comparative failure-rate evidence was not identified in this source set.</p>
<table class="mobile-card-table"><caption>Shared registry facts, with manufacturer scope and evidence limits</caption><thead><tr><th>Decision</th>{models.map(m=><th>{m.brand} {m.modelId}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{fields.map(([label,fn])=><tr><th>{label}</th>{models.map(m=><td>{fn(m)}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table>
<h2>Noise and consumption require their conditions</h2><p>Do not rank these brands from an isolated decibel or fuel-use number. Sound protocols can differ, and consumption points may use different delivered output on each fuel. Open the exact records for the published mode, distance, load percentage, units and unresolved fields.</p><ul>{models.map(m=><li><a href={'/models/'+m.slug+'/'}>{m.brand} {m.modelId}: full specification and source record →</a></li>)}</ul>
<h2>Service is a local question</h2><p>Ask who performs commissioning, how warranty claims are handled, what travel and diagnostic fees apply, and whether the provider services the exact model. We have not established comparable local response times or dealer-availability statistics; a nationwide marketing claim cannot answer those questions for your address.</p>
<h2>Bring both proposals onto the same scope</h2><p>Use the same backed-up loads, selected fuel, site constraints and desired operating priorities. Document exclusions for the meter, gas line, electrical upgrades, permits, cold-weather accessories and startup. Use the <a href="/planning/quotes/">three-quote comparison</a> to identify differences before judging totals. There is no automatic winner.</p>
</ArticleLayout>
